From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: cast insert_nulls values to float

_make_data(add_missing=True) runs every column, including the Int64
"group" column, through map_elements(insert_nulls,
return_dtype=pl.Float64), and insert_nulls hands back the original int.
polars up to 1.35 silently cast those ints to Float64; polars 1.36 and
later reject them while building the Series:

    polars.exceptions.SchemaError: unexpected value while building
    Series of type Float64; found value of type Int64: 0

so test_non_contiguous fails before reaching polars-ols. The oldest
polars available for riscv64 is 1.39, so no installable version still
accepts it. Return float(val), which is the cast older polars did
implicitly; the generated data is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against azmyrajab/polars_ols]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 tests/test_ols.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/test_ols.py b/tests/test_ols.py
--- a/tests/test_ols.py
+++ b/tests/test_ols.py
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
     if add_missing:

         def insert_nulls(val):
-            return None if rng.random() < 0.1 else val
+            return None if rng.random() < 0.1 else float(val)

         columns = missing_columns or df.columns
         df = df.with_columns(
